content:
 Go to the Launch Templates console and click Create launch template. Provide a name for the launch template. Navigate to My AMIs -&gt; Owned by me and select the AMI generated in the previous step. For the instance type, select t3.small and choose a key pair. Leave the subnet selection blank. Select the EC2 Security Group created in the previous step. Open a new browser tab to create a new IAM Policy that grants access permissions to fetch files from S3. Proceed to create a new IAM Role. Attach the required permissions to support the upcoming CI/CD pipeline. Here, attach AmazonSSMManagedInstanceCore, AWSCodeDeployRole, and the custom policy just created.
Return to the Launch Template setup wizard, expand the Advanced details section, and select the newly created role under IAM instance profile. Scroll down to the User Data field, insert the following script to ensure each newly provisioned instance pulls the latest deployment version, and click Create launch template.
#!/bin/bash cd /home/ssm-user/engexam docker compose pull docker compose up -d --force-recreate Through the steps above, the launch template has been successfully created.
